{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019sjh2PyCLpD7FD5LoJ1kUJ","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Product document for `scen-check-fix-records-term`.\n2\t#\n3\t# The catalogue phrases every step of E2E-001, and the glossary defines\n4\t# every term those phrases declare but \"reply\"; the fix adds the entry\n5\t# that defines it.\n6\t\n7\ttitle: \"Fixture host project\"\n8\t\n9\tdescription:\n10\t  summary: >-\n11\t    A single MCP service, used by the bdd-cli fixtures as the host\n12\t    project a scenario registry describes.\n13\t\n14\troles:\n15\t  - name: Operator\n16\t    definition: Runs the MCP service and watches what it answers.\n17\t  - name: Client Developer\n18\t    definition: Writes the clients that send the MCP service its requests.\n19\t\n20\tglossary:\n21\t  - term: mcp service\n22\t    means: >-\n23\t      The service this project builds: it takes a message from a client\n24\t      and answers it. What every Scenario of the project observes.\n25\t  - term: message\n26\t    means: >-\n27\t      One request a client sends the MCP service, as text. The service\n28\t      answers each message on its own.\n29\t\n30\tcatalogue:\n31\t  - template: 'the mcp service is running'\n32\t    block: given\n33\t    means: The MCP service has started and accepts requests.\n34\t    terms: [mcp service]\n35\t  - template: 'the {actor:role} sends \"{message}\"'\n36\t    block: when\n37\t    means: That role sends the quoted message to the MCP service, once.\n38\t    terms: [mcp service, message]\n39\t  - template: 'the service answers \"{reply}\"'\n40\t    block: then\n41\t    means: The MCP service's reply to the message is exactly the quoted text.\n42\t    terms: [mcp service, reply]\n43\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f073ef03-5bba-4608-b271-f45b41aa4ee8","uuid":"2c99b67e-45d8-40e3-8f05-436febdd46b0","timestamp":"2026-10-22T18:05:36.045Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"{{CWD}}/docs/product/p